UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wysiwyg prose line-clamp-14 overflow-hidden"><div><p>Become a civil engineer responsible for planning, designing and constructing projects that involve the built environment.<br/>From roads to railways, dams to harbors, houses to high-rises; civil engineers are responsible for the design and construction of all these assets. It is also civil engineers who work with other experts like builders, architects and clients to ensure that structures are safe, economical, and environmentally-sound. Students will learn how to prevent flooding, design irrigation systems and road infrastructure, and build multi-storeyed buildings. It is these skills that may see you specialize in structural engineering, geotechnical engineering, transport engineering, water engineering, or construction and infrastructure management.<br/>All online students are required to attend on campus block labs.</p></div><div><p style="font-weight:bold;">IT requirements</p><p>To do this course you’ll need a fast and reliable computer and access to high-speed internet. Expect to use about 5GB of data per month for every unit you’re doing. Find out more about the <a href="https://www.federation.edu.au/students/get-started/minimum-it-requirements/">minimum IT requirements</a> for studying with us.</p><h4>Got questions?</h4><p>Call us on 1800 333 864, start a live chat or <a href="https://www.federation.edu.au/contact/">submit an enquiry</a>.</p><h4>Student support</h4><p>The support we offer is second to none. Need academic help? No problem. Extra access or financial assistance? Let’s see what we can do. <a href="https://www.federation.edu.au/study/why-federation/support/">View our student services</a>.</p><h4>The fine print</h4><p>The commencement of all courses is subject to available funding and enrolment quotas.</p><p>Everything in this course overview is correct at the time of being published. However, the University reserves the right to alter any course, procedure or fee. Please check for changes before you apply or enrol.</p><p>Federation University uses Victorian and Commonwealth Government funding (for eligible students) to deliver training.</p><h4>School department</h4><p>Engineering</p></div></div>',
    total_course_duration = '4 years full-time or part-time equivalent480 credit points = 4.0',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '43500',
    entry_requirements = '<section class="accordionContainerBlock py-12 lg:py-16 !pt-6 lg:!pt-12 !pb-4 lg:!pb-8" data-blk="AccordionContainerBlock" id="entry-requirement"><div class="container mx-auto"><p class="fs-5xl mb-8 font-semibold text-primary" style="font-weight:bold;"><p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">Entry requirements</p></p><div data-orientation="vertical"><div class="border-b border-neutral-300" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed"><p class="flex" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" style="font-weight:bold;"></p><div aria-labelledby="radix-:rc:" class="!duration-500 overflow-hidden text-sm data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down data-[state=closed]:h-0" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" id="radix-:rd:" role="region" style="--radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width); transition-duration: 0s; animation-name: none; --radix-collapsible-content-width: 1027.21875px; --radix-accordion-content-height: 468px;"><div class="prose px-4 pb-8"><h4>Academic entry requirements</h4><p>Successful completion of Australian Year 12 with one final year course in Mathematics (any) or overseas equivalent.</p><h4>English language requirements</h4><p>Overall Academic IELTS band score of 6.0, with no band less than 6.0, or equivalent.</p><h4><abbr title="Australian Tertiary Admission Rank">ATAR</abbr></h4><p></p><p>Guaranteed ATAR: 60.00</p><p>Lowest Adjusted ATAR: 50.00</p><p></p><p>Applicable to onshore international students applying for undergraduate/bachelor degree programs only.</p></div></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical"><div class="border-b border-neutral-300" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="open"><p class="flex" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="open" style="font-weight:bold;"></p><div aria-labelledby="radix-:re:" class="!duration-500 overflow-hidden text-sm data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down data-[state=closed]:h-0" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="open" id="radix-:rf:" role="region" style="--radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width); --radix-collapsible-content-width: 1027.21875px; --radix-accordion-content-height: 604px;"><div class="prose px-4 pb-8"><p>If you’re an international student currently studying VCE in Australia, <a href="https://vtac.edu.au/">apply through VTAC</a>. If not, <a href="/link/10824d0d12ea4f57b870ef14178aad8b.aspx">find out how to apply directly to Federation University.</a></p><p>If you’re applying for a higher degree by research, make sure you <a href="/link/6efc37a41dd7457187d53a39c3475ba6.aspx">follow these instructions</a>.</p><p>Ready to fill out your application? You might need these codes:</p> <dl><dt><abbr title="Victorian Tertiary Admissions Centre">VTAC</abbr> application</dt><dd>Yes</dd><dt><abbr title="Victorian Tertiary Admissions Centre">VTAC</abbr> code</dt><dd>3700510113 - Mt Helen (on campus)</dd><dt>Direct application</dt><dd>Yes</dd><dt>Federation University code</dt><dd>EN8</dd><dt><abbr title="Commonwealth Register of Institutions and Courses for Overseas Students">CRICOS</abbr> code</dt><dd>116395A</dd></dl></div></div></div></div><div data-orientation="vertical"><div class="border-b border-neutral-300" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed"><p class="flex" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" style="font-weight:bold;"></p><div aria-labelledby="radix-:rg:" class="!duration-500 overflow-hidden text-sm data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down data-[state=closed]:h-0" data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" id="radix-:rh:" role="region" style="--radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width); transition-duration: 0s; animation-name: none; --radix-collapsible-content-width: 1027.21875px; --radix-accordion-content-height: 400px;"><div class="prose px-4 pb-8"><p>Applicants who meet a score of at least 20 in any English but do not meet the requirement for Mathematics can alternatively complete EDMTH1000 Introduction to Technical Mathematics unit offered by the Federation University Australia Pathways program prior to admission into the degree.</p><p>Admission pathways for applicants without a year 12 qualification</p><p>1.Completion of a Diploma of Engineering (Higher Education) at Federation University Australia</p><p>2.Completion of a cognate certificate IV in engineering in addition to a pathway mathematics unit “Introduction to Technical Maths” by Federation University Australia’s Foundation Access Studies (FAST) course</p><p>3.Completion of a cognate Diploma or Advanced Diploma in Engineering at a TAFE provider</p><p>4.Completion of Federation University Australia’s Foundation Access Studies (FAST) course</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.federation.edu.au/courses/den8.civ-bachelor-of-engineering-civil-honours',
    created_at = '2026-06-26 21:07:07',
    updated_at = '2026-06-26 21:07:07'
WHERE cricos_course_code = '116395A';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="wysiwyg prose line-clamp-14 overflow-hidden"><div><p>Invent new products, design innovative machines and change the way humans interact with mechanics.<br/>Become a professional engineer who is an expert in planning, designing, and managing engineering projects. Invent new products, design innovative tools, and change how humans interact with machines. Learn about energy by studying thermodynamics, and practice automation by exploring industrial robots. In your final year, pursue your interest area with your own unique engineering project.<br/>All online students are required to attend on campus block labs.</p></div><div><p style="font-weight:bold;">IT requirements</p><p>To do this course you’ll need a fast and reliable computer and access to high-speed internet. Expect to use about 5GB of data per month for every unit you’re doing. Find out more about the <a href="https://www.federation.edu.au/students/get-started/minimum-it-requirements/">minimum IT requirements</a> for studying with us.</p><h4>Got questions?</h4><p>Call us on 1800 333 864, start a live chat or <a href="https://www.federation.edu.au/contact/">submit an enquiry</a>.</p><h4>Student support</h4><p>The support we offer is second to none. Need academic help? No problem. Extra access or financial assistance? Let’s see what we can do. <a href="https://www.federation.edu.au/study/why-federation/support/">View our student services</a>.</p><h4>The fine print</h4><p>The commencement of all courses is subject to available funding and enrolment quotas.</p><p>Everything in this course overview is correct at the time of being published. However, the University reserves the right to alter any course, procedure or fee. Please check for changes before you apply or enrol.</p><p>Federation University uses Victorian and Commonwealth Government funding (for eligible students) to deliver training.</p><h4>School department</h4><p>Engineering</p><h4>Course co-ordinator</h4><p>Truong Phung</p></div></div>',
